@inherits LayoutComponentBase
@inject ICurrentUser CurrentUser

@* No nav, no footer. A phone acting as a buzzer should be the buzzer and nothing else.

   It still needs to know who is holding it, though. Identity used to come out of the URL here —
   /buzz/{code} — so this layout could get away with cascading nothing. Now that a code is
   exchanged for a session at /join/{code}, a page on this layout reads the cookie like every
   other page, and without the cascade it would see "Guest" and ask for a code it already has.

   Same shape as MainLayout: nothing renders until the identity resolves, because an IsFixed
   cascade is captured on the first render and never looked at again. *@
@if (_permissions is not null)
{
    <CascadingValue Value="_permissions" IsFixed="true">
        <main class="bare">@Body</main>
        <ToastHost />
    </CascadingValue>
}

@* Both of these are in MainLayout and neither was here, which meant a phone that threw showed
   nothing at all — no message, no reload link, just a screen that had quietly stopped. On the one
   kind of device in the building nobody can open developer tools on. *@
<div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
    Something went wrong.
    <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
    <span class="dismiss">🗙</span>
</div>

@code {
    private TripPermissions? _permissions;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() => _permissions = await CurrentUser.GetAsync();
}
